ervices. Qualifications: Master’s degree in criminal justice, forensic science, administration of justice or other criminal justice or related forensics degree required. Doctoral degree in the criminal justice or forensic science field preferred. Minimum of 3 years of experience with performing crime scene investigation, forensic photography, and fingerprint analysis required. Minimum of 1 year of higher education teaching adult learner experience required. Experience working in Law Enforcement required. Experience in developing course content preferred. Must be eligible to work in California to facilitate courses onsite at the Spectrum Campus in San Diego. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following by xxx. A cover letter. A curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body #LI-Onsite Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
