    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Fresno-Center-Fresno-CA/Campus-Support-Specialist_R20263531-1": {
      "title": "Campus Support Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $20.00 - $25.77 Position Summary The Campus Support Specialist provides on-site support for students and prospective students. Provides administrative support with academic advising, financial aid, student accounts, and university services. Acts as a liaison and first-level support for remote advising.  Essential Functions: Maintain all tasks/responsibilities set by the leadership team. Handle phone calls, in-person walk-ins, and emails from prospective students. Assist with student queries related to advising and university services. Organize and input information into databases. Plan and coordinate events with the Associate Center Director. Answer application and general enrollment inquiries from the public. Maintain excellent relations with students and prospective students. Maintain relevant records and documentation, as required. Provide input on how to improve processes based on client feedback. Properly assess students’ needs and determine the level of support needed. Perform other work-related duties like project planning and general administration as directed by the Associate Center Director. Update and analyze attendance rosters, enforcing National University attendance policies and procedures, initiate roster calls and retention procedures. Ensure daily or weekly communication updates to faculty, students, and staff by disseminating information through relevant channels and posting pertinent materials. Contribute to a positive and productive team atmosphere and working conditions. Deliver messages to students on behalf of the University as needed, not limited to above mentioned tasks. Ensure classroom, equipment, and facility is ready for daily activities including conferences, internal meetings, continuing education, and academic classes. Assist with room reservations. Support the campus or location in the absence of the Associate Center Director. Participate in ongoing department projects, or other special projects, as needed. Reasonable and consistent attendance to fulfill requirements of the position. Provide direct support and case management to students navigating academic and personal challenges, where on-camera participation during virtual appointments, team meetings, and cross-functional sessions is a fundamental component of effective communication, professional presence, and the quality of care students receive. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsi bilities :   N/A Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor's degree preferred or equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum of three (3) years of experience in customer service or related field required. Experience in higher education preferred . Experience working in a technology-driven enterprise preferre d. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Knowledge of University policies and procedures, including policy updates. Strong customer service skills and a desire to work in this capacity. Ability to manage difficult customer situations that may involve escalation. Established interpersonal skills and proven ability to work independently. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing as demonstrated by; expressing ideas and thoughts that are understood by others, exhibiting good listening and comprehension skills, and keeping others adequately informed. Skill in interacting with various departments. Strong ability to provide friendly service in-person, on calls, and in written correspondence regardless of message being delivered. Ability to remain solution-focused in all interactions with students, team members, clients, faculty, and staff, keeping in mind all University policies. Actively able to seek opportunities to influence, build effective relationships, and gain alignment with peers, functional partners, and/or external partners to accomplish business objectives.  Ability to multi-task and prioritize in a very fast-paced environment. Strong organizational, detail-oriented, and analytical skills. Ability to problem-solve, be flexible, meet deadlines, and adapt to an ever-changing environment. Strong administrative skills to facilitate operations.  Ability to maintain confidentiality. Must be able to consistently display the highest level of integrity. Ability to work well in teams while contributing to a positive and productive team atmosphere, working conditions, etc. Ability to advocate for students without compromising the integrity of the University. Strong understanding of the University mission, vision, values, goals, and strategies. Proficient with Microsoft Word and other applications in the Microsoft Office suite. Location: On-site Travel: Some Travel Required #LI-ONSITE Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Senior-Manager--Experimentation-Optimization_R20263526": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Experimentation Optimization",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $78,496.00 - $105,974.00 Position Summary The Senior Manager, Experimentation & Optimization leads conversion rate optimization (CRO) and experimentation for National University’s website and Digital experiences. This is a strategic, data-driven role responsible for defining and executing the CRO roadmap, proactively identifying optimization opportunities, and improving website experiences based on prospective student behavior, user insights, performance data, and lifecycle stage. The primary goal is to increase inquiry, application, and enrollment conversion through data-informed testing, continuous optimization, and an improved user experience. Essential Functions: CRO Strategy & Roadmap Own the CRO and experimentation roadmap for NU’s website and Digital experiences  including opportunity identification, intake, prioritization, sequencing and the testing calendar. Define, execute, and continuously optimize data-driven testing and optimization strategies that improve user experience, engagement, conversion, and content relevance across prospect-facing web experiences. Own website experimentation roadmap, related platform strategy, and associated vendor/partner relationships. Establish testing SLAs, QA standards, governance, and deployment practices that prevent conflicts across concurrent tests, campaigns, and releases. Maintain a repository of hypotheses, test results, learnings, optimization opportunities, and best practices that accelerate knowledge sharing and continuous improvement. Experimentation & Proactive A/B Testing Own the complete experimentation lifecycle: opportunity identification, hypothesis development, prioritization, test design, implementation, QA, launch, measurement, readout, and production rollout of winners. Proactively source the testing pipeline from behavioral analytics, session data, UX research, and website funnel diagnostics rather than operating as a request-driven queue. Design and run A/B, multivariate, and multi-page experiments, ensuring appropriate sample sizing, run length, and statistical significance before a result is acted on. Optimize information architecture, content presentation, navigation, page experience, and calls-to-action using customer insight and behavioral data. Translate experimentation outcomes into optimization recommendations that inform future website roadmaps, experience strategy, and investment priorities. Journey Discovery and Experience Optimization Analyze the end-to-end prospective student journey to identify friction, abandonment, and conversion opportunities using behavioral analytics, session replay, UX research, and customer feedback. Champion continuous optimization of program discovery across web properties, including on-site search, filters, navigation, program finders, and recommendation surfaces. Develop targeted website experience strategies using established audience segments, intent signals, engagement patterns, lifecycle stage, and experimentation insights to improve relevance, engagement, and conversion. Develop and optimize personalized website experiences that deliver relevant messaging, content, navigation, and recommendations based on audience needs, behavioral insights, and lifecycle stage. Partner with Marketing, Enrollment, and Digital Analytics to leverage audience segments, first-party customer data, and behavioral insights to support website personalization and optimization initiatives. Identify opportunities to apply AI-assisted optimization, predictive insights, and behavioral decisioning to improve relevance, engagement, and conversion outcomes. Participate and input into Journey Operations that impact Prospect Student experience in partnership with IT, Accounts, Brand and Product teams. Measurement, KPIs & Reporting Cadence Own measurement best practices, quarterly meta-analysis, CRO Playbook, dashboards, and the KPI framework supporting CRO, experimentation, and website personalization efforts. Define, monitor, and communicate KPIs including experimentation velocity, win rate, conversion improvement, inquiry conversion, application progression, website conversion, journey completion, personalization effectiveness, and incremental business impact. Establish and maintain a regular reporting cadence, including weekly program status, monthly CRO performance readouts, and quarterly roadmap and business-impact reviews for senior leadership. Build executive dashboards and communicate test results, KPI trends, roadmap progress, and strategic recommendations to the Chief Marketing Officer and senior stakeholders. Partner with the Digital Analytics team to establish analytical requirements, measurement plans, and dashboard reporting for UX. Measure the maturity of National University’s experimentation program and continuously evolve optimization capabilities through data-driven insight. Innovation & Continuous Improvement Evaluate emerging trends in AI, personalization, experimentation, behavioral science, and digital experience optimization. Identify opportunities to incorporate intelligent personalization, predictive experiences, and innovative optimization capabilities into National University’s prospective student website experiences. Evaluate new technologies, platforms, and optimization capabilities that strengthen website audience engagement, experience effectiveness, and conversion performance. Continuously benchmark industry trends, competitor experiences, customer expectations, and evolving digital behaviors to identify future opportunities for innovation and growth. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsi bilities : Individual contributor role that provides leadership through influence and expertise; scope may evolve over time based on organizational needs. Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Business, Analytics, Statistics, Human-Computer Interaction, or a related field. Master’s degree or M.B.A. preferred. 7 + years of experience in conversion rate optimization and experimentation, website experience management, personalization, digital merchandising, or e-commerce. 2+ years of experience in a strategy, program ownership, or related manager responsibilities. Demonstrated ownership and administration of A/B testing and personalization platforms (Adobe Target, VWO, Optimizely, or equivalent), including governance, implementation oversight, and optimization best practices. Experience designing, implementing, and optimizing personalized digital experiences using audience segmentation, behavioral targeting, geo-targeting, and journey-based experience targeting. Proven experience developing and executing a CRO and experimentation roadmap, including KPI development, prioritization frameworks, and executive reporting. Experience managing vendors, agency partners, and external development resources to deliver experimentation, personalization, and digital optimization initiatives. Demonstrated track record of leveraging experimentation and personalization strategies to drive measurable improvements in conversion, lead generation, engagement, and business outcomes. Experience in higher education, edtech, or another complex, high-consideration, multi-audience environment preferred. Portfolio, case studies, or documented examples demonstrating measurable conversion improvements and successful optimization initiatives across complex digital ecosystems. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Deep expertise in experimentation methodologies, including hypothesis development, test design, statistical analysis, and interpretation of results to support business decisions. Strong experience leading conversion rate optimization (CRO), personalization, and digital experience optimization programs at scale. Expertise with experimentation, personalization, and analytics platforms such as Adobe Target, Optimizely, VWO, Adobe Analytics, GA4, and FullStory. Strong understanding of customer data platforms, audience segmentation, behavioral targeting, and customer journey optimization. Ability to independently analyze, validate, and interpret complex datasets using SQL, dashboards, and analytics tools to identify opportunities and inform strategy. Experience developing experimentation roadmaps, success metrics, governance processes, and executive reporting frameworks. Strong understanding of UX principles, customer journey mapping, and the integration of qualitative and quantitative insights into optimization strategies. Knowledge of accessibility (WCAG), responsive design principles, content strategy, and technical considerations impacting experimentation and personalization. Experience evaluating and applying emerging technologies, including AI-driven personalization, predictive modeling, and automated decisioning. Exceptional communication, storytelling, stakeholder management, and executive presentation skills, with the ability to translate data into actionable business recommendations. Demonstrated ability to influence and build alignment across Marketing, Product, UX, Technology, Analytics, Enrollment, and other cross-functional teams without direct authority. Strategic mindset with the ability to balance long-term vision, customer needs, operational realities, and measurable business outcomes while driving complex initiatives to completion. Location: Remote, USA Travel: up to 10% travel Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Senior-UX-Strategist_R20263517-1": {
      "title": "Senior UX Strategist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $78,496.00 - $105,974.00 Position Summary The Senior UX Strategist is responsible for shaping and optimizing end-to-end customer experiences across the prospective student journey through research, journey strategy, customer discovery, service design, and innovation. This role leads user research, journey mapping, design thinking, and requirements gathering to uncover customer needs, identify experience opportunities, and translate insights into actionable strategies and scalable solutions. Working cross-functionally with Product, Design, Analytics, Marketing, and Technology teams. The Senior UX Strategist drives alignment, influences decision-making, and helps create customer-centered digital experiences that improve engagement, conversion, and overall user outcomes. Essential Functions: Experience Strategy & Journey Mapping Lead end-to-end prospective student journey mapping, service blueprinting, and experience strategy initiatives across National University's digital ecosystem. Define current-state and future-state prospective student journeys, identifying friction points, unmet needs, moments that matter, and opportunities to improve engagement, inquiry, application progression, and enrollment outcomes. Translate prospective student insights, institutional priorities, and business objectives into experience strategies, journey roadmaps, and prioritized recommendations that influence digital product and UX roadmaps. Develop experience frameworks, journey principles, and future-state vision artifacts that guide customer-centered digital experiences across the prospective student lifecycle. Partner with Marketing, Enrollment, Product, and Digital teams to align prospective student journey priorities with institutional goals and long-term digital strategy. User Research & Discovery Develop and own the UX research strategy and roadmap supporting prospective student experience initiatives. Lead and execute qualitative and quantitative research, including stakeholder interviews, prospective student interviews, usability testing, surveys, concept validation, diary studies, and behavioral research. Synthesize customer insights, behavioral analytics, market research, competitive analysis, and voice-of-the-customer findings into strategic recommendations that shape experience strategy and digital priorities. Establish and mature UX research standards, repositories, tools, governance, and knowledge-sharing practices that strengthen organizational understanding of prospective student behaviors and needs. Manage research vendors, participant recruitment, research operations, budgets, and external partnerships to ensure high-quality research execution. Partner with the Digital Analytics team to combine qualitative and quantitative insights into a comprehensive understanding of prospective student behaviors, motivations, and decision-making. Innovation, Ideation & Experience Planning Lead design thinking workshops, customer journey workshops, ideation sessions, and cross-functional innovation initiatives focused on improving the prospective student experience. Facilitate collaborative discovery sessions with Product, Marketing, Engineering, Analytics, Enrollment, and Content teams to identify customer needs, define opportunities, and align on future-state experiences. Gather, synthesize, and prioritize business, customer, and technical requirements, translating findings into strategic experience recommendations, opportunity assessments, and implementation-ready requirements. Develop future-state journey concepts, service blueprints, experience frameworks, and innovation proposals that improve prospective student engagement and enrollment outcomes. Research emerging trends in customer experience, AI, higher education, and digital innovation to identify new opportunities that strengthen National University's prospective student experience. Influence digital product and experience roadmaps by advocating for prospective student needs, journey improvements, and evidence-based experience decisions. Supervisory Responsi bilities : Individual contributor role that provides leadership through influence and expertise; scope may evolve over time based on organizational needs. Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Business, Analytics, Statistics, Human-Computer Interaction, or a related field. Master’s degree or M.B.A. preferred. 6 -8 years of experience in UX Strategy, UX Research, Service Design, Customer Experience, or Product Discovery. Experience leading journey mapping, customer research, design thinking workshops, requirements gathering, and cross-functional facilitation. Experience managing research vendors and UX research platforms. Experience designing for higher education, edtech, or other multi-audience environments preferred. Strong portfolio demonstrating user-centered design across complex digital ecosystems. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Deep expertise in qualitative and quantitative research methodologies, customer discovery, experience strategy, and human-centered design principles. Strong experience translating customer insights, behavioral data, and business objectives into strategic recommendations, journey roadmaps, and experience investments. Advanced facilitation, storytelling, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to lead workshops, align diverse perspectives, and build consensus across complex organizations. Expertise in journey mapping, service blueprinting, experience ecosystems, design thinking, and innovation frameworks. Ability to synthesize customer research, market intelligence, competitive analysis, and business priorities into actionable strategies that influence product, marketing, enrollment, and digital experience decisions. Demonstrated ability to influence senior leaders and cross-functional teams through customer insights, strategic thinking, and evidence-based recommendations. Experience developing future-state vision artifacts, experience principles, opportunity frameworks, and strategic roadmaps that guide organizational decision-making. Familiarity with UX research platforms and collaboration tools (User Testing, Userlytics, Dovetail, Miro, Figma, Qualtrics, etc.). Strong understanding of experimentation frameworks, behavioral analytics, conversion optimization, and data-informed experience design practices. Solid understanding of accessibility (WCAG), responsive design principles, content strategy, and digital experience best practices. Exposure to AI, personalization, emerging technologies, and digital innovation trends, with the ability to evaluate their impact on customer experience and business outcomes. Strategic mindset with the ability to balance long-term vision, customer needs, organizational objectives, and execution realities. Exceptional written, verbal, and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with executives, stakeholders, and cross-functional teams. Ability to work independently, lead through influence, navigate ambiguity, and build strong partnerships across a diverse and matrixed organization. Demonstrated commitment to accountability, continuous improvement, collaboration, and customer-centered decision-making. Location: Remote, USA Travel: up to 10% travel #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Los-Angeles-Center-Los-Angeles-CA/Part-time-Faculty--Applied-Behavioral-Analysis_R20263468-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Applied Behavioral Analysis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: Applied Behavioral Analysis (Hybrid) Location: Hybrid – Los Angeles National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Position Summary The Department of ABA, School Psychology, and Ed Counseling, in the Sanford College of Education at the National University invites applications for part-time faculty in Applied Behavioral Analysis. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of or potential for excellence in teaching in their field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. The successful candidate will have the potential for a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position primarily works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success. Essential Job Duties: Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. Qualifications: Masters ( MA or MS) degree in the field of Applied Behavioral Analysis or related field from a regionally accredited university required. 2 years of higher education teaching experience preferred. Must hold BCBA for a minimum of 5 years and be in good standing with the BACB required. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following: A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. #LI-Hybrid Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Part-time-Postdoctoral-Fellow_R20263508": {
      "title": "Part-time Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89 Position Summary The School of Social and Behavioral Sciences (SSBS) at National University seeks applications for a 9-month Postdoctoral Fellow in either the Department of Marriage Family Sciences (DMFS). Fellows will have the opportunity to teach and learn in an online environment within a proven and evolving educational model. At National University, diversity and inclusivity are our greatest strengths and essential to good decision-making. Accordingly, we are keenly interested in supporting and mentoring a diverse pool of postdoctoral fellows. We strongly encourage applications from women and minorities. Postdoctoral Fellows in the SSBS teach graduate courses within a programmatic core discipline as assigned. Primary responsibility is to engage students, offer excellent feedback, and inspire students to achieve course and program outcomes relevant to the core discipline. Postdoctoral Fellows also come into the position with a proposal for professional scholarship and growth opportunities they want to pursue during the experience. This position works closely with other faculty teaching in the discipline, Associate Director of Faculty Support and Development, Department Chair, and Dean. Essential Functions: The role of Postdoctoral Fellow may include teaching courses within a programmatic core discipline as assigned. In addition, the following points will be discussed as part of the hiring process: Demonstrate a commitment to NU’s vision, mission, and goals and those of the School of Social Behavioral Sciences. Promote a graduate culture of scholarship, teaching, service, and practice. Demonstrate commitment to and capacity for Teaching through Engagement and using the NU One-to-One, apprenticeship style teaching model. Participate in research and scholarship opportunities congruent with teaching load and Department expectations. Pursue opportunities for service to the profession as appropriate. Engage in relevant professional practice activities congruent with teaching load and Department expectations. Teach masters and/or doctoral courses in the DMFS. Participate in initial and ongoing training. Participate in trial use of new technologies and integrates new technologies into their teaching. Participate in school-specific and university postdoctoral networking meetings. Maintain contact with students via phone, video conferencing, and email through their courses. Work collaboratively with Academic and Finance Advisors to ensure student engagement and success. Exercise academic freedom in teaching course content and achieving learning outcomes in accordance with University policy, procedures, and curricula. Participate in program and student assessment procedures. Perform all educational services in accordance with NU policies and procedures, the Family Education Rights to Privacy Act, National University’s Code of Conduct and all other state and federal laws. Tasks and projects as assigned by the Dean or NU administrators. Reasonable and consistent attendance to fulfill requirements of the position. Supervisory Responsi bilities : N/A   Requirements: Education & Experience: Doctoral degree from a regionally accredited institution with academic qualifications in an area aligned with the mission and offerings of the Department of Marriage and Family Sciences required. Experience teaching, working with, and mentoring diverse students strongly preferred. Experience in graduate level coursework and clinical training preferred. Proficiency in the use of technology in the delivery of education and online teaching experience are preferred. Curriculum development experience preferred. Experience working in a technology-driven enterprise preferred. Professional identity as a couple/marriage and family therapist Graduation from a COAMFTE accredited program strongly preferred. AAMFT Clinical Fellow and Approved Supervisor desirable. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following. A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Part-time-Faculty--Master-of-Nursing---Psychiatric-Mental-Health-Nurse-Practitioner--PMHNP-_R20263482-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Master of Nursing - Psychiatric-Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $52.84 - $69.81 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: Master of Nursing - Psychiatric-Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) Location: Remote, USA National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Position Summary The Department of Nursing, in the School of Health Professions at the National University invites applications for part-time faculty in Nursing with a specialization in Psychiatric-Mental Health Nurse Practitioner. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of or potential for excellence in teaching in their field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. The successful candidate will have the potential for a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position primarily works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success. This is an excellent opportunity for a Part-Time Faculty to join our highly engaged faculty in Nurse Practitioner program. As an integral and vital part of our teaching staff, the successful candidate will provide students with unique and valuable perspectives by helping them to develop critical thinking, communication, and therapeutic nursing skills within the framework of transcultural nursing. Essential Job Duties: Efficiently deliver didactic and/or clinical instruction online to students. Plan and deliver an effective “classroom” experience through Zoom, that promotes learning of course/program learning objectives and prepares the student to be a competent, beginning Nurse Practitioner. Effectively engage students, utilizing a variety of teaching methods. Evaluate students in classroom and clinical settings utilizing effective educational methods and tools. Grading assignments and responding to student inquires within 48 hours of assignment submission. Responding to student inquires via email within 24 hours of receipt of the email, thus providing timely feedback to students' questions and concerns. Communicate effectively with students, staff, and faculty, both verbally and through written communication. Focus on student-centered learning in all aspects of curriculum. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Master of Science in Nursing, Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner, or Doctor of Nurse Practitioner with a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner specialization. Active, current, and unencumbered PMHNP state license in either Texas or California required within 6 months of employment. Please see the Licensing Requirements section below for more details. Minimum of two 2 years’ current experience in a PMHNP role, including diagnosing and treating patients in a clinic setting. National board certification - PMHNP specific. Online higher education experience. Demonstrated experience in developing and maintaining courses. Preferred Qualifications: Doctor of Nurse Practitioner with a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner specialization. Experience with the following course topics is preferred: Introduction to Psychotherapy, Introduction to Psychotherapy Practicum, MH Care: Adults/Aging Adults, MH Adults/Aging Adults Practice. Licensing Requirements: To teach in this program, faculty are required to hold an active, current, and unencumbered PMHNP state license in California and Texas. Candidates must agree to obtain licenses in both California and Texas within 6 months of employment if they are not currently licensed in these states. Candidates will be given consideration if they meet at least one of the following requirements: Hold an active, current, and unencumbered PMHNP state license in California or Texas. Once hired, faculty are required to have both RN and FNP licenses in both California and Texas. The department will pay for new faculty to obtain their license in either California or Texas if the applicant holds one but not the other. Hold an active, current, and unencumbered PMHNP state-issued license from a state(s) other than California or Texas, and have an active application to obtain either a California or Texas license. The department will pay for new faculty to obtain their license in either California or Texas – whichever state the candidate is not already in the process of obtaining. Both California and Texas licenses must be obtained within the first 6 months of employment. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following. A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Los-Angeles-Center-Los-Angeles-CA/Part-time-Faculty--Bachelor-of-Science-in-Nursing--Clinical-Site-Assignments--Obstetric-and-Mother--Baby-Nursing--Los-Angeles--CA-_R20263498-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Bachelor of Science in Nursing, Clinical Site Assignments, Obstetric and Mother, Baby Nursing (Los Angeles, CA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $52.84 - $69.81 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: Bachelor of Science in Nursing – Clinical Site Assignments – Obstetric & Mother–Baby Nursing (Los Angeles, CA) Location: Onsite: Los Angeles, CA National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Position Summary The Department of Nursing, in the School of Health Professions at National University, invites applications for part-time faculty to conduct Obstetric & Mother–Baby Nursing clinicals at placement sites for the Bachelor of Science in Nursing program. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of, or potential for excellence in, teaching in their field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position primarily works with the Academic Program Director along with other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and student success. Essential Job Duties: Lead sessions at clinical placement sites. Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. Some indirect patient care is also performed in the skills and simulation lab. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: A Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from a regionally accredited institution.   At least one year of continuous clinical bedside nursing experience in an acute care setting (Obstetric & Mother–Baby Nursing) within the last 5 years as a RN providing direct patient care, OR at least one year of RN level clinical teaching experience within the last 5 years. Must have a current, unencumbered CA Registered Nursing license. Preferred Qualifications: Terminal degree (Ph.D., DNP, or Ed.D.) from a nationally accredited or regionally accredited university. 2+ years of higher education teaching experience in a professional nursing program. Experience teaching adult learners. National certification in specialty area. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following. A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. Location: Onsite: Los Angeles, CA #LI-Onsite Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
