      "title": "Part-time Faculty, California Master of Arts in Counseling Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: California Master of Arts in Counseling Psychology Location: Hybrid – Spectrum (San Diego, CA) National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Position Summary The Department of Masters in Arts Counseling, in the JFK School of Psychology and Social Sciences at the National University invites applications for part-time faculty . The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of or potential for excellence in teaching in their field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. The successful candidate will have the potential for a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position primarily works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success. Essential Job Duties: Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. Qualifications: Doctoral degree (Ph.D., Psy.D.) or Master's degree in Counseling, Counseling Psychology, Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Social Work, or in a related field of psychology from a regionally accredited university, with a current License in California. 3 years of higher education teaching experience preferred. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following. A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body #LI-Hybrid Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Part-time-Advanced-Practice-Nurse_R20253145": {
      "title": "Part-time Advanced Practice Nurse",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $60.00 - $65.00 National University’s School of Health Professions, in collaboration with the School of Education, invites applications for a uniquely rewarding Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) position within a long-term, grant-funded initiative serving elementary school communities across San Diego. This role is ideal for an FNP who values meaningful patient interaction, interdisciplinary teamwork, and community-centered care. You will join a highly collaborative, close-knit group of healthcare professionals who are passionate about equitable access, preventive care, and whole-family wellbeing. Position Highlights Part-time, flexible scheduling: Work two-three days per week, Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday. Family-centered clinical practice: Provide care not only to elementary school students, but also to their parents and siblings. a rare opportunity to support holistic family health in a school-based setting. Low daily patient volume: Typically 5–8 patients per day (with the higher end occurring infrequently), allowing for 45-minute visits and the ability to deliver thorough, relationship-based care. Integrated health education: When clinic volume is lower, engage with students in the classroom, teaching preventive care, mental health awareness, and the relationship between physical and emotional wellbeing. Community impact: Participate in one Saturday Community Health Fair per month on a rotating basis, as well as occasional after-school community events. Weekly hours flex accordingly—for example, working two 4-hour days during the same week to accommodate Saturday or after-school coverage. Hybrid work potential: On-site coverage from 8:00–8:45 a.m. start time through  3:00 p.m. , with remaining hours available to be completed remotely. Grant-funded stability: Funding is secured through 2029, offering long-term consistency within a mission-driven program. What Makes This Role Special A supportive team environment with strong communication, shared resources, and a true commitment to community health. The ability to practice at a thoughtful pace, building real relationships with families. A balanced clinical and educational scope that enables you to influence health literacy from an early age. A schedule that supports work–life balance and flexibility. Requirements: Education & Experience: Graduate of an accredited school of nursing with an earned Master of Science in nursing degree. Graduate of an accredited Nurse Practitioner Program. Current Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) Certification and Licensure as a Registered Nurse. Current California Furnishing number, NPI and current DEA registration number. Hold and maintain current national and state board certification as a nurse practitioner from approved organization (American Nurses Credentialing Center, American Academy of Nurse Practitioner, National Certification Corporation for Obstetrics, Gynecologic and Neonatal Nursing Specialty). Current certification in Basic Life Support (BLS), Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS), and PALS. Recent experience in an advanced practice nurse role. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Publisher, Outlook, SharePoint, Adobe and Peoplesoft. Knowledge of office policies and procedures, and strong organizational skills. Strong interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment with frequently changing priorities. Strong analytical skills and attention to detail and accuracy. Demonstrated interpersonal skills to work cooperatively with diverse individuals; proven ability to communicate professionally. Works well independently, possesses the ability to take direction, work as a team player, and maintain confidentiality. Location: Onsite at designated school site locations. Travel: Up to 75% travel to ensure clinical practice consistency across all clinic locations. #LI-Onsite Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Veteran-Education-Benefits-Assistant---VA-Work-Study_R20263489-1": {
      "title": "Veteran Education Benefits Assistant – VA Work Study",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: : $16.90 - $16.90 Position Summary The Veteran Education Benefits Assistant supports National University’s (NU) School Certifying Official (SCO) team in providing accurate and timely assistance to students using Veterans Education Benefits. They will work closely with SCO team leadership to identify military-affiliated student needs and participate in campus initiatives that support Veteran Services (e.g., Veteran Center Food Pantry). The VEB Assistant will attend webinars, student orientations, and on-campus training seminars related to VA Education Benefits. Additional responsibilities may include other tasks related to on-campus Veteran Services as assigned. Location:  Hybrid, Spectrum Center, San Diego, CA Essential Functions: Fields Veteran Education Benefits inquiries in person, by phone, and virtually. Assists with reporting student enrollments to the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs. Process VA correspondence and support other administrative tasks related to the administration of Veteran Education Benefits. Perform other duties as assigned to support the effective delivery of on-campus Veteran Services. Requirements: Current NU student receiving Veteran Education Benefits under Title 38, U.S.C., Chapters 30, 31, 32, 33, 35, 1606, and Edith N. Rogers STEM Scholarship. Enrolled in and pursuing an approved program of education at a rate of 3/4 time or greater during the work study semester. Maintain good academic standing according to NU’s Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) Policy. Ability to meet National University’s employee performance and campus dress code standards. Experience in customer service and customer relations. Technical / Functional Skills : Fundamental understanding of Veterans Education Benefits. Ability to navigate VA.gov, Ask VA, eBenefits.gov, and the GI Bill® Comparison Tool. Proficiency in communicating within hybrid work environments. Basic computer skills with experience using Microsoft Office Suite. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Ability to complete projects in a timely manner. Note :   Veterans with service-connected disabilities rated at 30 percent or more are given hiring priority for VA Work Study positions. #LI-DNI   Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
