    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Full-time-Assistant-Professor-in-Clinical-Mental-Health_R20263549": {
      "title": "Full-time Assistant Professor in Clinical Mental Health",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $66,560.00 - $75,066.00 National University – San Diego, California Assistant Professor in Clinical Mental Health – Remote, USA The Department of Counseling Psychology and Social Work, in the John F. Kennedy School of Psychology and Social Sciences at National University, invites applications for an Assistant Professor in the Clinical Mental Health program. Rank is commensurate with qualifications and experience . The successful candidate will have the potential for excellence in teaching and scholarship in the counseling field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position is remote. This position works closely with other faculty within the discipline and administration contributing to programmatic strategies that ensure program quality, student engagement, and success. We are looking for a candidate who can collaborate with faculty, program leadership, and operations staff to support the delivery of comprehensive, high-quality academic and clinical training experience for students. While the primary function of this role is teaching and requires the ability to teach across various courses, it also integrates service, scholarship, and clinical training experience to support student development and program excellence. The Assistant Professor reports to the Department Chair and works closely with CMHC leadership to ensure alignment with programmatic goals and accreditation standards, including those established by CACREP. Essential Functions Candidates will be evaluated for their level of proficiency and potential (for excellence) in teaching, scholarship, and service. The main expectations of this position include: Teaching Teach and develop online courses in the area of clinical mental health in content areas of counseling theories, assessment and testing, and diagnosis and treatment. Teach clinical courses and participate in Final Presentations. Maintain pedagogical and subject matter expertise in the instructor’s field. Create an inclusive and positive learning environment for diverse learners. Ensure course and program practices align with compliance and accreditation standards. Adhere to the National University’s academic integrity policy. Scholarship Maintain a productive scholarship agenda suitable to a teaching university. Engage in scholarly activities to maintain professional growth with counseling organizations such as the American Counseling Association. Participate in professional development as outlined in faculty policies. Service Support school and program leadership on accreditation reviews. Consult on program processes and participate in discussions to improve and innovate the CMHC program. Provide regular opportunities to offer academic guidance and mentorship to individual CMHC students on training process and placements, program requirements, development of practicum and career goals, and any problems/concerns that they encounter throughout the tenor of their program. Participates in any remediation processes involving CMHC students. Serve as a reviewer of all program materials to ensure compliance with CACREP and state standards. Collaborate and provide support to internal stakeholders on appropriate data collection, analysis, evaluation, and dissemination of reports including the regular evaluation of the students’ comportment and experience quality. Serve a faculty advisor for student organizations such as CSI and faculty point of contact for student programming such as new student orientation, graduation celebration, etc. Maintain professional communication with internal and external stakeholders. Participate in administrative meetings and project teams as requested. Complete all other tasks and/or projects as assigned.  Maintain membership and actively participate with professional counseling organizations such as the American Counseling Association. The ideal candidate will possess the following qualifications : Education & Experience Doctoral degree in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited institution/program required. Licensed or license eligible as a professional counselor (LPC) required. Strong identification with professional counselor identity and evidence of such, e.g., membership in professional counselor organization(s), licensing activities, conference attendance, etc., required. 2+ years of faculty experience in a program in a CACREP accredited CMHC program and/or clinical training administration experience in a CACREP accredited CMHC program preferred. Experience with CACREP accreditation and compliance as well as ability to assist in management of such preferred Experience teaching online courses in asynchronous format; experience working in a technology-driven enterprise preferred. Curriculum development experience preferred. Special conditions of employment include: Background check required. Travel is required at least once annually to attend the annual Commencement ceremony (if held onsite). For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following: A cover letter that includes interest in the position and brief summary of required qualifications met. A curriculum vita Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Human-Resources-Associate_R20263581": {
      "title": "Human Resources Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $30.63 - $39.82 Position Summary With general supervision, the Human Resources Associate provides comprehensive support and response for the daily operations of the Human Resources Business Partner team by executing Human Resources (HR) policies and procedures, initiating resource planning, and maintaining interdepartmental communication. Partners with HRBPs to provide support to clients by building credible and trusted relationships with business leaders. Provides support for human resource transactions including document management, HRIS entry, recruitment, employee relations, performance management, and special projects.  This role is positioned within a highly functioning HR team with a focus on relationships, culture, talent development, data interpretation, goals, and initiatives. The goal is to ensure the HR department's operations run smoothly and effectively to deliver maximum value to the organization as a whole. Essential Functions: Performs supportive and routine tasks to support Human Resources Business Partners (HRBPs) and client groups. Partners with HRBPs and leaders to support business goals as necessary. Supports HRBPs and leaders in researching and compiling information and metrics to facilitate HR strategy and support HRBP client groups.  Act as the first point of contact for employee queries on policy related topics. Responds in a timely manner and provides updates, as needed, to internal and external customer inquiries. Coordinates employee onboarding in conjunction with Talent Acquisition, the HR Business Partner, and the hiring manager. Maintains compliance with federal, state, and local employment laws and regulations, and recommended best practices; reviews policies and practices to maintain compliance. Maintains knowledge of trends, best practices, regulatory changes, and new technologies in human resources. Ensure employee files and records are stored in appropriate electronic format. Enhance employee satisfaction by resolving issues promptly. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsi bilities : N/A Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Human Resources Management, or related field, required. Two (2) to four (4) years’ of experience as a Human Resources professional required. Or equivalent combination of education and experience PHR/SHRM-CP preferred. Experience providing service to a remote workforce preferred. Experience in higher education preferred. Experience working in a technology-driven enterprise preferred. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Working knowledge of Federal, State and local employment laws and human resource principles, practices and processes.  Ability to organize documents and workflow. Accepts personal accountability, proactively seeks resolution for personal limitations head-on; and supports honesty and respect towards others, the company and oneself.   Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Excellent interpersonal, negotiation, and conflict resolution skills. Ability to effectively maintain relationships with faculty, staff, and leadership.  Ability to actively listen to clients’ circumstances, issues, expectations and needs using patience, attentiveness and positivity, and attention to details. Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing to appropriately communicate with a wide range of individuals of constituencies in a diverse community.  Excellent organizational and time management skills with a proven ability to work in a fast-paced environment with multiple deadlines and frequently changing priorities.  Proactive self-starter, taking full ownership of HR initiatives and promptly implementing solutions while continuously updating key business stakeholders on progress. Intermediate knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite Applications such as Word, Excel, Power Point, Outlook and Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) software related to Human Resources Information Systems. Location: Remote, USA Travel: No Travel Required #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
