    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/MultiUse-Lab-Assistant-Supervisor--Spectrum-Center-_R20263574": {
      "title": "MultiUse Lab Assistant Supervisor (Spectrum Center)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $20.00 - $25.77 Position Summary Assist the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director in the overseeing of the Multiuse laboratories in support of National University academic programs.  Provides technical support to the Mulituse laboratories at the campuses. Work closely with university staff, faculty and students to ensure a positive teaching and learning experience. Under the supervision of the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor ensure compliance with OSHA / EPA / California regulations and safety requirements. Assist with supervision, training, and coordination of the work schedule of the Multiuse Laboratory Assistant(s) and/or Technician(s). Maintains a positive team environment, leading the team when the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director is not present, providing reporting and class preparation support for team members, driving results, and coaching to outcomes for the team. In addition, is the first point of contact for students and organizational escalations. Essential Functions Act as the auxiliary supervisor for all Multiuse Laboratories within the National University System. Supervise the preparations for laboratory experiments and demonstrations for scheduled classes in close collaboration with university faculty. Assist with and train multiuse laboratory staff on experiment set-ups. Assist instructors and students during laboratory classes. Provide monthly and long-term laboratory schedules to campus directors, SoALS and resolve scheduling conflicts. Develop a hands-on operating guide for the SeqStudio genetic analyzer, and keep it updated when forensic procedures change. Develop a hands-on operating guide for the Ultra Performance Liquid Chromatography (UPLC) for chemical separation and analysis.    Add procedures for confirmatory testing of when chemical materials are added to the forensic curriculum.    Provide guidance to Facilities, SoALS, and Campus Operations on laboratory design/workflow when new laboratories are added or when existing laboratories are updated. Guidance could include equipment lists, pricing, water/electrical requirements, laboratory safety equipment requirements, and storage requirements. Follow policies and procedures for good laboratory practices. Maintain consumable and perishable components to OSHA / EPA standards. Assist with and train multiuse laboratory staff and instructors on experiment set-ups and outcomes. Assist with and train multiuse laboratory staff, professors, and students in the proper disposal of HAZMAT / BIOHAZ materials. Train multiuse laboratory staff on the Medical Waste Management Plan, SDS use and maintenance, chemical storage, and inventories, chemical and bio-hazardous disposal, logs, and laboratory safety, I.A.W, National University policies. Ensure multiuse laboratory staff understand and comply with the proper handling and storage of hazardous materials and human pathogens per OSHA / EPA regulations and standards. Ensure the laboratory is maintained in good working order. Emphasis on neatness, cleanliness, stocked reagents bottles, and all equipment is in good working order. Perform depot level maintenance on all microscopes, clean lenses, correct adjustment on ocular lenses, clean & align condenser, repair stage, and change light assembly. Perform periodic maintenance on SeqStudio Genetic analyzer, Polaris Q mass spectrophotometer (MS), Trace gas chromatograph (GC), and UPLC per the manufacturer’s guidelines.  Contact the manufacturer if warranty repairs are needed. Order, store, and maintain a current and complete inventory of laboratory supplies. Replenish stock, as needed.  Export packaged courses to other university campuses. Manage projects and deadlines set by the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director to ensure timely progression and completion. Provide team member training support. Identify current team and individual challenges to provide early intervention for team member improvement.  Maintain team member coaching log and provide feedback to Associate Director for annual evaluations and regular 1:1s. Provide escalation support and first level conflict resolution.  Lead department meetings. Hold 1:1s with team members and provide skills coaching. Team oversight and coverage support in the absence of the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director Remediation committee team member for performance management. Maintain the highest level of integrity and professionalism. Coach and provide feedback for team members on lab and chemical preparation and safety Support front line team members through safety changes as well as course changes and all things involved with being able to teach those courses Oversee team member engagement in class as necessary when expectations are not being met. Provide support and coverage for team as needed. Participate in ongoing department projects, or other special projects, as needed. Reasonable and consistent attendance to fulfill requirements of the position. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsi bilities :   Indirect oversight of up to 6 front line team members. Coaching, performance support and feedback, outcome delivery, process management, and team member training required. Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor's degree in science-related field of study required; and, two to four (2-4) years of experience in science laboratory techniques and concepts in the areas of life, physical, and forensics sciences, safety regulations and procedures in science laboratories. Manage teams of technicians at the Spectrum, South Bay, Naval Hospital, Fresno, and Los Angeles locations. Provide lab technicians training on the operation and maintenance of all laboratory equipment using written, Zoom sessions, and onsite visits. Provide training on Aseptic techniques, bacterial culturing, and sterile bacterial media preparation to all technicians. Ensure technicians know how to interpret course syllabi and laboratory schedules to provide timely laboratory preparation and setups. Operation and maintenance of SeqStudio Genetic Analysis, UPLC chromatography, PCR, electrophoresis, physiology workstations, microscopes, FT-IR and UV-VIS spectrophotometry. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Ability to effectively and efficiently communicate organizational goals and deadlines to team members. Ability to create a positive and productive work environment. Ability to provide support in the hiring and training process of new team members. Ability to coach to skill improvement and outcome development. Strong understanding of all degree programs, specializations, and courses. Ability to stay current via self-study on university policies, including policy update In-depth knowledge of science laboratory procedures, safety and chemical hygiene plans and small spill clean-up. Ability to conduct internet search and requisition for laboratory supplies, chemicals, and equipment. Strong understanding of Natural Science and science laboratory operations/vernacular. Strong written and verbal skills, organization, and follow-through. Attention to detail. Ability to use science laboratory tools and equipment required to support a typical university level academic environment/curriculum. Function as university laboratory operations and safety expert and achieve compliance with external and internal safety policies and procedures. Achieve compliance with regulations regarding storage/use/disposal of HAZMAT and BIOHAZ material. Establish new vendor contracts and maintain current vendor agreements and warranties. Solves problems and develops relationships through shared goal of providing optimum learning environment for university students. Ability to participate as an active team member of the team and organization and work toward a common goal. Accepts personal accountability, proactively seeks resolution for personal limitations head-on; and supports honesty and respect towards others, the company and oneself. Work independently and foster a cooperative spirit within a large and/or small team of diverse cultures, while working in a fast-paced environment with multiple projects, deadlines, and frequently changing priorities. Location: Onsite, Spectrum Center Travel: May be required to other National University campuses with a multiuse laboratory and other areas to assess new locations for a laboratory.   #LI-Onsite Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Director--Registrar-Operations_R20263584": {
      "title": "Director, Registrar Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $71,360.00 - $96,340.00 Position Summary: The Director of Registrar Operations provides strategic leadership and operational direction for core functions within the Registrar’s Office. This role is accountable for maintaining the accuracy, integrity, and security of student records, ensuring compliance with academic and institutional policies, and overseeing the effective execution of key services, including registration and scheduling, degree auditing, transfer articulations, transcript evaluations, and graduation. The Director leads initiatives to elevate service quality, streamline processes, and support the university’s mission and strategic objectives. Exercising a high degree of independent judgment, the Director is expected to conduct in-depth analysis, evaluate operational effectiveness, and provide data-informed recommendations to guide improvements and ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations Essential Functions: Provides day to day leadership, guidance, and direction to Associate Directors overseeing student records, evaluations and articulation, scheduling, and graduation Oversees the hiring and recruiting process within the Registrar’s Office and supports Associate Directors, in the onboarding and training process Support and provide professional development, coaching, and performance management of Associate Directors and their teams Oversees, tracks, and assists with all performance management and disciplinary action procedures Oversees the daily operations of all departments within the Registrar’s Office including records and processing, evaluations and articulations, scheduling, graduation, and student requests and appeals Ensure timely, accurate, and compliant execution of core registrar functions, including academic records management, course scheduling, transcript and enrollment processing, degree evaluation, and conferral. Foster cross-departmental collaboration and serve as a liaison with academic and administrative stakeholders to support institutional initiatives. Provides support to Academic Leadership and faculty to streamline processes, collaborate on key initiatives, and  problem solve new challenges or changes Collaborate with the University Registrar to develop and implement strategic initiatives that enhance operational effectiveness and student-centered services Generates and analyzes weekly and monthly reports to monitor departmental performance, leveraging key metrics to identify trends and provide insights to leadership Establish and monitor performance metrics, service level standards, and continuous improvement efforts across all operational areas Utilizes data and trend analysis to inform strategic decision-making, evaluate departmental performance, and identify opportunities for growth, efficiency, and enhanced student service delivery Attend meetings/training as needed to further job skills and knowledge Assist with the daily processes of the Registrar’s Office as needed, including CRM software to monitor the department's email inbox as assigned and communicating with students and other departments within the university Verify requests for dates of attendance and degrees awarded; authenticates claims and documents; identifies suspected fraudulent documents and reports to the University Registrar. Make determination regarding eligibility of petition utilizing University catalog, CAS Manual and Business Process Guide (BPG). Acts as liaison with CAS members, faculty, department chairs, and deans to obtain timely resolution of CAS petitions as needed Perform liaison functions between Registrar, Financial Aid, Student Services, Academics, Finance, and Regional Operations Directors to assure timely resolution to CAS and LOA requests. Responsible for reporting on and improving system processes while working collaboratively with respective Functional Analysts in the enhancement of student services Lead process improvement projects and systems optimization efforts, particularly within student informatio systems and related platforms Participate in testing of functionality for university-wide system upgrades Interpret and apply academic policies, FERPA regulations, and accreditation standards, ensuring compliance and consistency across all registrar operations Research and analyzes current industry standards and best practices related to enrollment, scheduling, grade, and attendance reporting. Evaluates methods to increase output and accuracy. Creates, oversees, and implements plans for approved changes Manage the development of admission and registration processes, procedures and practices including recommendations to the academic councils for changes required Monitor DOE Title IV polices, changes, and requirements and analyze university policy on LOA with the viewpoint of assuring compliance. Responsible for noting persistent problem areas or patterns of problems in relation to institutional academic policies that occurs within a region, learning center, or by individual staff members, and provide possible solution(s), so issues can be resolved Identify, develop, implement, and assess technological solutions to processes and procedures surrounding the university policy exceptions and LOA policies. Analyze submitted student requests for patterns in policy application to provide recommendations for policy modifications Develop expertise in both Registrar Office and Financial Aid Office areas of SOAR to facilitate knowledge and understanding of Title IV regulations, R2T4 calculations, and the policies and practices on withdrawal as implemented at the university. Responsible for ensuring accurate enrollment reporting to National Student Clearinghouse for students on LOA or students approved via CAS for class drop/withdrawal status Collaborate with University wide divisions (Student Services, Academics, Finance) related to policy implementation and adherence in relation to exceptions to policy and appeal decisions Provides detailed expert guidance and assistance to students, staff, faculty, and administration regarding LOA and CAS decisions. Analyzes and assesses student academic and non-collegiate records to ensure eligibility and application of student course waivers, course substitutions and transfer credit utilizing teach-out plans, approved crosswalks, and current CAS exceptions Participate in ongoing department projects, or other special projects, as needed Reasonable and consistent attendance to fulfill the requirements of the position Other duties as assigned Supervisory Responsibilities : Direct leadership and oversight up to 3 Associate Directors with up to 3 team leads and up to 35 front line staff team members Hire train, and develop leaders and staff members Implement and lead individualized development plans for all team members Direct oversight for all performance management actions inclusive of direct coaching, performance management and action delivery, and separation of staff members Support leaders within the department on preparation, review, and delivery of all required performance evaluations Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree required. Master's degree preferred. Minimum of seven (7) years related experience in higher education Minimum of five (5) years of leadership experience required Minimum of three (3) years of leadership experience in a Registrar’s office preferred. Experience in higher education required. Experience working in a technology-driven enterprise preferred. All skills, abilities, and education will be considered for minimum qualifications. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Serves as a role model by anticipating and planning for change Effectively communicates a clear vision to the team to foster alignment and direction Demonstrates strong leadership by influencing others to achieve results, using creativity and strategic thinking Ability to understand, diagnose and plan for business issues, processes, structure, outcomes, and profitability. Understands the implications of decisions and actions. Deep understanding of overall big picture of the business; able to take an idea from concept to reality Actively seeks opportunities to influence, build effective relationships and gain alignment with peers, functional partners and/or external partners to accomplish business objectives. Ability to maintain job related, social and organizational and ethical norms Accepts personal accountability, proactively seeks resolution for personal limitations head-on; and supports honesty and respect towards others, the company and oneself. Collaborate with others to ensure the best results for the team and company. Ability to reach out and ask for help or seek expertise of others when needed Excellent working knowledge of Title IV guidelines as applicable with the ability to successful fact-based decisions and use sound judgment Advanced use of computers and Microsoft Office Suite Applications such as Word, Excel, Power Point, Outlook, and software application used in student evaluation record including imaging processes, Optical Character Recognition and Electronic Document Management software such as OnBase Ability to work independently and efficiently under pressure of deadlines Ability to work in close proximity to others in a congenial and supportive environment. Excellent oral and interpersonal communication skills and ability to communicate effectively with senior administration, staff and faculty. Possess mature judgment with ability to be tactful and diplomatic in difficult student and staff/faculty encounters Proficient in Microsoft Suites Experience with Salesforce, PeopleSoft, and Anthology Location: Remote, USA Travel: Some travel required, about 10% #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Human-Resources-Technology-Analyst_R20263492": {
      "title": "Human Resources Technology Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $62,579.00 - $84,480.00 Position Summary As a member of the HR Technology team, this individual will manage the design, development, testing, deployment, and maintenance of custom Workday reports and dashboards in alignment with organization’s HCM tenant configuration, HR program goals, and data security framework. He/she will work with internal clients, including senior management, to define reporting requirements, improve customer experience, and generate value for stakeholders across a broad base using Workday’s various reporting tools. In addition to HCM, the scope includes payroll, benefits, time tracking, compensation, performance, recruiting, and Organizational Talent and Development. Collaborate with subject matter experts to maximize system functionality and the ability to produce reliable, accurate information for HR reporting, planning, regulatory, and forecasting purposes. Organize and manage HR data across multiple affiliates in the National University System while providing guidance and support to HR and organizational leaders on HR data. Essential Functions: Provide support activities, including research, issue resolution, and support of training initiatives within Workday. Conduct projects such as mass system updates, business process improvement, and employee records management. Conducts complex audits and performs specialized reconciliations to ensure data integrity, accuracy, and compliance, on a regular basis. Collaborates with HR team and key stakeholders to recommend, design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain custom Workday reports and dashboards for meaningful metrics, trends, and analytical insights. Maintain documentation of existing processes and procedures to facilitate ongoing upkeep, continuous improvement, and compliance with regulatory requirements. Troubleshoot existing reports and dashboards to solve issues as reported by end users related to access, design, configuration changes, and releases while ensuring security and data privacy standards. Build, maintain, and support integrations to other internal and external systems involving internal and external stakeholders, as appropriate. Provide analysis of impacts to reporting based on new releases or updates to system functionality and recommend/apply changes in addition to reporting and dashboard related testing for each release Supports the preparation of effective and high-quality presentations to clearly communicate findings, insights, and recommendations related to HR data. Review emerging system trends for potential updates to system or platform functionality and best practices. Maintain awareness of data security and comply with policies and procedures while partnering with internal customers to ensure data and security consistency across all reporting platforms Other duties as assigned Supervisory Responsi bilities: N/A Requirements Education & Experience BA/BS degree in computer science, information systems, human resources, or related discipline preferred. Two-three years of related professional experience in a role that relies heavily on data administration and analysis. Workday configuration/administration (HCM, integrations, Workday Studio, security, business processes, recruiting, payroll, absence, time, compensation, dashboards). Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Working knowledge of current Human Resources, Payroll, Benefit and legal principles and parameters MS Suite (advanced knowledge of Microsoft Excel, including pivot tables, lookups, formulas, and graphs required) Able to maintain confidentiality and judgement in handling sensitive, critical, private, proprietary and protected information. Able to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with a high attention to detail and accuracy. Data visualization and communication of complex information to non-technical audiences. Business process analysis and auditing Excellent interpersonal and communication skills while interacting with individuals at all levels of the organization. Understanding of information systems architectures and technology platforms. Able to navigate ambiguity and work under tight timelines and changing priorities. Self-starter with a passion for problem solving. Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment leveraging agile methodologies. Tech savvy with excellent analytical skills, able to work across multiple HR technologies. Travel: Minimal Location: Remote, USA #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
